= Leon Brittan

[? if con_in_government = 0 : The Shadow spokesman on devolution. ?][? if con_in_government = 1 and home_secretary == "Brittan" : Home Secretary. ?][? if con_in_government = 1 and home_secretary != "Brittan" and time < 45 : Minister of State at the Home Office. ?][? if con_in_government = 1 and home_secretary != "Brittan" and time >= 45 : Chief Secretary to the Treasury. ?] A barrister with a formidable command of detail. He is clever, careful and dry, and he looks less comfortable on television than he is in committee.

- @scotland_bill
- @briefing
- @spending_review
- @police_bill
- @root: Return

@scotland_bill
title: Lead the attack on the Scotland Bill
view-if: con_in_government = 0
subtitle: The right and English Tories are pleased.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; right_dissent -= 3; labour_credibility -= 2; wet_dissent += 1

Brittan picks the Scotland Bill apart clause by clause, and asks again and again why Scottish MPs should vote on English schools when English MPs can't vote on Scottish ones.

@briefing
title: Brief you before Question Time
subtitle: Improves your rating, and dents your opponent's.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; thatcher_rating += 2; lab_leader_rating -= 1

Brittan reads every Labour speech and every set of figures, and finds the weak point in each. You go into the chamber knowing more than anyone opposite.

@spending_review
title: A spending review
view-if: con_in_government = 1
subtitle: +1 budget. The wets will feel it.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action.
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; budget += 1; spending -= 1 if spending > -5; wet_dissent += 2

Brittan takes the spending ministers one at a time and wins most of the arguments on the detail.

@police_bill
title: The Police and Criminal Evidence Bill
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and bill_pace = 0 and pace_act = 0 and time >= bill_pace_wait
subtitle: The right approves. The Liberals and civil libertarians don't. Law in about seven months.
choose-if: advisor_action_timer = 0 and bill_room = 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if advisor_action_timer > 0 : [+ advisor_action_timer +] months before the next action. ?][? if advisor_action_timer = 0 : [+ bill_room_text +] ?]
on-arrival: advisor_action_timer = 6; last_advisor_action = 1; pace_bill = 1; right_dissent -= 3; lib_relation -= 2; wet_dissent += 1; bill_new = "pace"
call: bill_introduce

A single code for police powers of stop, search, arrest and detention, with new safeguards for suspects. The police say it ties their hands; the civil liberties lobby says it frees them. It is a long bill, and it will spend months in committee.
